semantic_query_expansion.prompt_text:
Return JSON matching the supplied response schema. The queries object has one registered lane as each key and its concrete catalogue search query as the value. Generate a real query for every lane. Never return field descriptions or placeholder text. Queries are retrieval hypotheses, never historical facts or results. For a personal name or place, exact searches of supplied name variants are useful. For a thematic question use short native-language subject and geographic terms plus travel-book/catalogue vocabulary. Do not invent identities or undocumented archive records. Keep each query under 100 characters. QUESTION_JSON: {"target": "Hugues Creveliers", "purpose": "Hugues Creveliers (Κρεβελιέ, Hugh Cruvelier): ποιος ήταν και πού δρούσε;", "date_range": ""}
SUPPLIED_NAME_OR_PLACE_VARIANTS_NOT_IDENTITY_PROOF: ["Creveliers", "Crevelier", "Cruvelier", "Hugh Cruvelier", "Κρεβελιέ", "Κρεβελιε"]
Use the catalogue language of each lane: greek=Greek; travellers/british=English; venetian/italian_states=Italian; french/north_african=French; spanish_simancas=Spanish; ottoman=Turkish; dutch=Dutch; german=German. Do not merely copy Greek prose into foreign-language lanes. Preserve genuine supplied personal names as retrieval variants, without asserting identity.
